    "body": "Reviewed. The resplit analysis reproduces exactly from the committed checks (I re-ran trialguide.eval.resplits on them and got the same summary), and tests pass. The README is clear about the Kaggle re-run not matching the cluster run. Two suggestions:\r\n\r\nThe λ̂ shift from 0.766 to 0.562 on the same frozen commit is a finding in itself (risk control is sensitive to small numeric differences between machines with only 26 calibration patients). It deserves a line in the top-level README results, not only here.\r\nIn “How to read this”, say plainly that on the Kaggle checks λ̂ = 0.562 is the lowest candidate, i.e. it accepts every inference, so the conformal step does not bind on this run. The verdicts README says it; this one should too.\r\nApproving.",
